{"name":"Wind of Change","hex":"#c8deea","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"wind","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Real or perceived movement of atmospheric air usually caused by convection or differences in air pressure.","Air artificially put in motion by any force or action."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To blow air through a wind instrument or horn to make a sound.","To cause (someone) to become breathless, as by a blow to the abdomen, or by physical exertion, running, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wind"},{"term":"change","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become something different.","To make something into something else."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The process or result of becoming different.","Small denominations of money given in exchange for a larger denomination."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/change"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yashwantrao Chavan","blocks":[{"text":"Yashwantrao Balwantrao Chavan was an Indian independence activist and politician who served as 5th Deputy Prime Minister of India in the short-lived Charan Singh ministry in 1979. He served as the last Chief Minister of Bombay State and the first of Maharashtra after the latter was created by the division of Bombay State. His also held significant ministerial post was as the 8th Minister of Finance from 1970 to 1971 and from 1971 to 1974."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Yashwantrao_Chavan_2010_stamp_of_India.jpg/330px-Yashwantrao_Chavan_2010_stamp_of_India.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yashwantrao_Chavan"},{"title":"Warriors (novel series)","blocks":[{"text":"Warriors, also known as Warrior Cats, is a children's and young adult fantasy novel series about feral cats living in a forest. It is published by HarperCollins and written under the collective pen name Erin Hunter. Its nine subseries (\"arcs\") chronicle the survival and adventures of five organized groups of feral cats, called Clans, as they interact with each other and outsiders."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d0/Warriors_full_boxed_Set.png/330px-Warriors_full_boxed_Set.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warriors_(novel_series)"},{"title":"Wind of Change (Scorpions song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Wind of Change\" is a song by German rock band Scorpions, recorded for their 11th studio album, Crazy World (1990). A power ballad, it was composed and written by the band's lead singer, Klaus Meine, and produced by Keith Olsen and the band. The lyrics were composed by Meine following the band's visit to the Soviet Union at the height of perestroika, when the enmity between the communist and capitalist blocs subsided concurrently with the start of large-scale socioeconomic reforms in the Soviet Union."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7a/Wind_of_Change_European_artwork.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind_of_Change_(Scorpions_song)"},{"title":"Wind","blocks":[{"text":"Wind is the natural movement of air or other gases relative to a planet's surface. Winds occur on a range of scales, from thunderstorm flows lasting tens of minutes, to local breezes generated by heating of land surfaces and lasting a few hours, to global winds resulting from the difference in absorption of solar energy between the climate zones on Earth. The study of wind is known as anemology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif/330px-Cherry_tree_moving_in_the_wind_1.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wind"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Y_B_Chavan.jpg/500px-Y_B_Chavan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Y_B_Chavan.jpg/1280px-Y_B_Chavan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Y_B_Chavan.jpg/500px-Y_B_Chavan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chavan with his family.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AY_B_Chavan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg/500px-Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg/1280px-Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg/500px-Alder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The New Forest in Hampshire, an inspiration for the setting of Warriors","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlder_trees_beaulieu_river_fawley_ford.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Tencent_Video_Warriors_animated_series_artwork.jpg/330px-Tencent_Video_Warriors_animated_series_artwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Tencent_Video_Warriors_animated_series_artwork.jpg/330px-Tencent_Video_Warriors_animated_series_artwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Concept art for the animated series","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATencent_Video_Warrio